    {
      "id": "505:553",
      "name": "ComponentLab/ToolBoxItem",
      "properties": {
        "Label#505:15": {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "defaultValue": "General"
        },
        "Show icon#505:16": {
          "type": "BOOLEAN",
          "defaultValue": false
        },
        "Show mnemonic#505:17": {
          "type": "BOOLEAN",
          "defaultValue": false
        },
        "Icon#974:21": {
          "type": "INSTANCE_SWAP",
          "defaultValue": "973:43",
          "preferredValues": []
        },
        "State": {
          "type": "VARIANT",
          "defaultValue": "Default",
          "variantOptions": [
            "Default",
            "Hover",
            "Selected",
            "Focus",
            "Disabled"
          ]
        }
      },
      "description": "Classification: ComponentLab/ToolBox is the Native Component (QToolBox → commonWidget::Z_ToolBox). ToolBoxItem is internal design-system visual anatomy, not a standalone Qt QWidget or SDK public component. Selected previews the host currentIndex (writable int Q_PROPERTY); per-item Disabled is configured by setItemEnabled(index, bool), not an Item checked Q_PROPERTY. Focus and Hover are transient visual previews. Qt owns page widgets and currentChanged.\n\nQt QToolBox item contract. State variants support Label, Show icon, Icon and Show mnemonic. Icon is an INSTANCE_SWAP semantic glyph; host State owns the nested vector color override (Disabled→Disabled, otherwise Primary), so the replacement icon&#39;s standalone Tone is intentionally overridden. Page ownership, currentIndex, insertion/removal and mnemonic dispatch remain runtime-owned.\n\nAsset contract: Default, Hover and Focus use fixed ComponentLab/Icon/ChevronRight; Selected uses ChevronDown with Accent semantics; Disabled uses ChevronRight with Disabled semantics. The general Icon slot remains independently swappable, while expansion, currentIndex, mnemonic dispatch and accessible expanded state remain runtime-owned.\n\nSource verification · 2026-10-08: native-components.json generates commonWidget::Z_ToolBox, whose wrapper only inherits QToolBox and sets the three design-system identity properties. NativeComponentRegistry can create it and ComponentLab NativeGalleryPages exercises two basic pages. The current Z_ToolBox.qss.in contains root, root:disabled and a repeated root border rule only—no QToolBox::tab selected, hover, disabled, focus or mnemonic coverage—and no dedicated ToolBox contract test was found. Factory availability is verified; single-current navigation, complete tab styling, keyboard behavior and accessibility remain engineering-open."
    }
